 60GA dE EAV,LOGFT$From BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 60GA c  2021Or01: {+60}Ge was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 60GA2c  345-MeV/u {+78}Kr primary beam impinging on a 5-mm thick {+9}Be target,
 60GA3c  identified in the RIKEN BigRIPS separator by B|r-|DE-ToF, transported  
 60GA4c  to the exit of the ZeroDegree spectrometer, and implanted into the     
 60GA5c  Wide-range Active Silicon Strip Stopper Array for Beta and ion         
 60GA6c  detection (WAS3ABi) consisting of three 1-mm-thick DSSDs. A total of   
 60GA7c  1.5E4 60Ga ions were implanted. |g rays were detected using the        
 60GA8c  EUroball-RIKEN Cluster Array (EURICA) of 12 cluster-type Ge detectors. 
 60GA9c  Measured E{-p}(>0.9 MeV), E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, and
 60GAAc  implant-decay correlations. Deduced decay scheme, decay branching      
 60GABc  ratios, {+60}Ge T{-1/2}, and {+60}Ge mass using A=60 he isobaric       
 60GACc  multiplet mass equation(IMME).                                         
 60GA c  2016Ci01: {+60}Ge was produced in fragmentation of a 150-MeV/nucleon   
 60GA2c  {+78}Kr{+34+} primary beam impinging on a {+9}Be target, transported   
 60GA3c  through the NSCL A1900 fragment separator, and implanted into the      
 60GA4c  optical time projection chamber (OTPC). A total of 41 {+60}Ge ions were
 60GA5c  implanted. Measured {+60}Ge T{-1/2} and |e+|b{++}-delayed protons.     
